Bloodmarkers is a tool to organise your own lab data. It is not a medical
device and it does not give medical advice. AI output can be wrong.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party content and data
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

LOINC
  The biomarker catalogue in supabase/seed.sql contains LOINC codes, and the
  optional script scripts/loinc/import-loinc-terms.ts loads the LOINC table you
  download yourself.

  This material contains content from LOINC (https://loinc.org). LOINC is
  copyright (c) Regenstrief Institute, Inc. and the Logical Observation
  Identifiers Names and Codes (LOINC) Committee and is available at no cost
  under the license at https://loinc.org/license. LOINC(R) is a registered
  United States trademark of Regenstrief Institute, Inc.

NEVO (Dutch food composition database, RIVM)
  Not included in this repository. scripts/seed-nevo.ts loads the NEVO CSV
  that you download yourself from https://www.rivm.nl/en/dutch-food-composition-database
  after accepting the RIVM conditions of use. Those conditions require the
  source reference shown in the app ("Food data: NEVO (RIVM)") and do not
  allow charging end users for the use of NEVO data.

Open Food Facts
  The nutrition features query the Open Food Facts API at run time. Open Food
  Facts data is available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0,
  https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/.

DUTCH
  "DUTCH" (Dried Urine Test for Comprehensive Hormones) is a test by Precision
  Analytical, Inc. This project is not affiliated with Precision Analytical.
  The DUTCH reference values in supabase/seed.sql are labelled
  "dutch-sample-report": they are placeholders based on a sample report, not
  official ranges. Use the ranges printed on your own report.

Reference ranges
  The reference ranges in supabase/seed.sql are general adult ranges for
  orientation only. Ranges with source "optimal-functional" or
  "functional-medicine" are opinions from integrative-medicine literature
  without a single cited source. Your lab's own ranges take priority.
